(6455412, 957334, 124457, '<td valign="top">It is tough working with children, even your own. I had to move fast and didn''t have alot of time to set up the camera. I thought it was a great concept that missed in the delivery. I really needed another adult to work the kids. I snapped about 15 shots with a remote in my hand then reframed the shot and snapped 10 more. Only one, the last one, was the remote out of the picture. The kids were done so I had to go with it. I wanted some things you see on a table when people are having a drink together. It''s a tea party, so cell phones for everyone, sunglasses, plates with desserts and purses on the bench seat.  Each daughter wanted thier own tea set so it is cluttered. The scattered legos in the foreground were to represent a car crash type of link to the bottle for irresponsible drinking. low light on me like a dimly lit bar, I just wish the couch wasn''t there but something more of a barlike look to give a transition. Bright and colorful on what is important, my girls. I''m looking at the lego shot glass as a kind of acceptance to the sacrifices that are made for being a responsible parent that can still have fun. Too bad my daughter on the left side looked away at the tv and had a binky in her mouth. I''m traing them to play to the camera so they will get better and so will I. Thanks for all your kind comments.<br/></td>', 'It is tough working with children, even your own. I had to move fast and didn''t have alot of time to set up the camera. I thought it was a great concept that missed in the delivery. I really needed another adult to work the kids. I snapped about 15 shots with a remote in my hand then reframed the shot and snapped 10 more. Only one, the last one, was the remote out of the picture. The kids were done so I had to go with it. I wanted some things you see on a table when people are having a drink together. It''s a tea party, so cell phones for everyone, sunglasses, plates with desserts and purses on the bench seat.  Each daughter wanted thier own tea set so it is cluttered. The scattered legos in the foreground were to represent a car crash type of link to the bottle for irresponsible drinking. low light on me like a dimly lit bar, I just wish the couch wasn''t there but something more of a barlike look to give a transition. Bright and colorful on what is important, my girls. I''m looking at the lego shot glass as a kind of acceptance to the sacrifices that are made for being a responsible parent that can still have fun. Too bad my daughter on the left side looked away at the tv and had a binky in her mouth. I''m traing them to play to the camera so they will get better and so will I. Thanks for all your kind comments.', '2011-06-29 01:37:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6455413, 957961, 96664, '<td valign="top">I think this one is under appreciated... I love the smoke it the back!<br/>Knowing how hard you worked on this I looked you up and found it. Well done but I think it was for sure underrated...</td>', 'I think this one is under appreciated... I love the smoke it the back!Knowing how hard you worked on this I looked you up and found it. Well done but I think it was for sure underrated...', '2011-06-29 01:37:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6455422, 957246, 28742, '<td valign="top">Great finish, Lydia! I''m sure you can''t help but wonder where this would have landed if you could have gotten that frog to drink! :)</td>', 'Great finish, Lydia! I''m sure you can''t help but wonder where this would have landed if you could have gotten that frog to drink! :)', '2011-06-29 01:48:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6455429, 957334, 124457, '<td valign="top">I can''t remember if I used a flash. I don''t normally use a flash when I have time to set the camera but because the kids and I were in the shot I set it to auto so the flash may have gone off creating more shadows. The room has what some friends call french fry lights, recessed lighting in the ceiling which caused some shadows too. I have some hot lights but without help I could not set them up. There was alot of light in the picture, the white plates were blown out and so were alot of the tea set objects before editing.</td>', 'I can''t remember if I used a flash. I don''t normally use a flash when I have time to set the camera but because the kids and I were in the shot I set it to auto so the flash may have gone off creating more shadows. The room has what some friends call french fry lights, recessed lighting in the ceiling which caused some shadows too. I have some hot lights but without help I could not set them up. There was alot of light in the picture, the white plates were blown out and so were alot of the tea set objects before editing.', '2011-06-29 01:51:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6455441, 957945, 28742, '<td valign="top">Only thing I can see that might hurt this (even though it may not be reflected in the comments) is the crop. In the context of an Absolut ad, you wouldn''t crop the bottle. And in the context of the humor of a squirrel drinking vodka, it seems like it would work better if it wasn''t so tight. I''m guessing there might have been no choice because of other things in the photo or maybe you framed it this tight. I gave the shot an 8 and didn''t really notice the crop issue til now, although I feel like it may have influenced me subconsciously. Anyway, just my opinion. Hope it''s useful.</td>', 'Only thing I can see that might hurt this (even though it may not be reflected in the comments) is the crop. In the context of an Absolut ad, you wouldn''t crop the bottle. And in the context of the humor of a squirrel drinking vodka, it seems like it would work better if it wasn''t so tight. I''m guessing there might have been no choice because of other things in the photo or maybe you framed it this tight. I gave the shot an 8 and didn''t really notice the crop issue til now, although I feel like it may have influenced me subconsciously. Anyway, just my opinion. Hope it''s useful.', '2011-06-29 01:56:44.000000', NULL, 0),
